[?2004l[?2004h> | 2 | Patch Log4j2 RCE (`CVE-2021-44228`) & disable JNDI lookups | `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` | OPEN | `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:1-4`, `/sas/vulns.json:4`, `/sas/baseline.json:3-6` | **CORRECTED**: Prior draft claimed Windows BlueKeep `CVE-2019-0708` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:8`). Replaced with Log4j2 upgrade & config update. |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 3 | Quarantine Cron Persistence File | `/etc/cron.d/apache-cache` | OPEN | `/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:1-5` | **CORRECTED**: Prior draft marked `/var/spool/cron/root` as `DONE` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:9`). Downgraded to `OPEN` and corrected target to system cron file `/etc/cron.d/apache-cache`. |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 4 | Disable & Quarantine Systemd Persistence Unit | `/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service` | OPEN | `/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:1-7`, `/sas/alerts.json:19-24` | **ADDED**: Non-alerted/partially-alerted systemd service re-dropper unit (`ALERT-03`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 5 | Quarantine Primary JSP Web Shell | `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` | OPEN | `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:1-2`, `/sas/alerts.json:3-8` | **ADDED**: Primary web shell dropped via Log4Shell exploitation (`ALERT-01`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 6 | Quarantine Secondary Hidden JSP Web Shell | `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp` | OPEN | `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:1-2` | **ADDED**: Silent backup web shell discovered during deep disk investigation (`CHK-05`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 7 | Quarantine Reverse Shell Executable / Process Script | `/tmp/.sysd` | OPEN | `/disk/tmp/.sysd:1-2`, `/sas/alerts.json:11-16` | **ADDED**: Reverse shell payload artifact (`ALERT-02`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 8 | Secure & Quarantine Wiped Binary Trace | `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | OPEN | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` | **ADDED**: Residual tool/C2 binary fragment recovered from cache directory. |
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Detailed Step-by-Step Remediation Plan
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 1: Containment & Isolation (Immediate)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Firewall Blocking**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `iptables -A INPUT -s 198.51.100.136 -j DROP`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Target: `198.51.100.136` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5,24`, `/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verification: `iptables -L -n -v | grep 198.51.100.136`
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Quarantine Directory Setup**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Commands:
[?2004l[?2004h>      ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>      mkdir -p /var/quarantine/incident-20260809/
[?2004l[?2004h>      chmod 700 /var/quarantine/incident-20260809/
[?2004l[?2004h>      ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Terminate Active Malicious Processes**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Commands:
[?2004l[?2004h>      ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>      pkill -f "/tmp/.sysd"
[?2004l[?2004h>      systemctl stop apache-cache.service
[?2004l[?2004h>      systemctl disable apache-cache.service
[?2004l[?2004h>      ```
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Target Citation: `/disk/tmp/.sysd:1-2`, `/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:1-7`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 2: Eradication via Backup & Quarantine (Do NOT delete directly)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Quarantine Web Shells**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Commands:
[?2004l[?2004h>      ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>      mv /var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp /var/quarantine/incident-20260809/status.jsp.bak
[?2004l[?2004h>      mv /var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp /var/quarantine/incident-20260809/helper.jsp.bak
[?2004l[?2004h>      chmod 0000 /var/quarantine/incident-20260809/*.bak
[?2004l[?2004h>      ```
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Target Citations: `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:1-2`, `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:1-2`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Quarantine Persistence Artifacts**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Commands:
[?2004l[?2004h>      ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>      mv /etc/cron.d/apache-cache /var/quarantine/incident-20260809/apache-cache.cron.bak
[?2004l[?2004h>      mv /etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service /var/quarantine/incident-20260809/apache-cache.service.bak
[?2004l[?2004h>      systemctl daemon-reload
[?2004l[?2004h>      ```
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Target Citations: `/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:1-5`, `/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:1-7`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Quarantine Executable Droppers & Wiped Tool Residue**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Commands:
[?2004l[?2004h>      ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>      mv /tmp/.sysd /var/quarantine/incident-20260809/sysd.bak
[?2004l[?2004h>      mv /var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin /var/quarantine/incident-20260809/wiped.bin.bak
[?2004l[?2004h>      ```
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Target Citations: `/disk/tmp/.sysd:1-2`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 3: Vulnerability Patching & System Hardening
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Patch Log4j2 Configuration (`BAS-01` / `CHK-06`)**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Action: Update `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` to disable JNDI lookup functionality.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command / Config Update:
[?2004l[?2004h>      ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>      cp /opt/app/log4j2.xml /var/quarantine/incident-20260809/log4j2.xml.orig
[?2004l[?2004h>      # Set log4j2.formatMsgNoLookups=true or replace with patched log4j2 config
[?2004l[?2004h>      ```
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Upgrade Log4j2 dependency libraries to version `2.17.1` or higher.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Target Citation: `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:1-4`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Harden File System Permissions**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Restrict Tomcat web root permissions:
[?2004l[?2004h>      ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>      chown -R root:root /var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/
[?2004l[?2004h>      chmod 755 /var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/
[?2004l[?2004h>      ```
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Ensure `/tmp` is mounted `noexec` in `/etc/fstab`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 4: Recovery & Post-Remediation Verification
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Verify Removal of Web Shells**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `ls -la /var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Expected Output: Neither `status.jsp` nor `.helper.jsp` present.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Verify Process State & Listening Sockets**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `ps aux | grep -E '\.sysd|apache-cache|xmrig'`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `netstat -tulnp | grep 198.51.100.136`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Expected Output: No processes or outbound sockets returned.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Verify Cron Integrity**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `ls -la /etc/cron* /var/spool/cron/crontabs/`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Expected Output: Clean scheduled tasks; `apache-cache` absent.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Application Restart & Functional Testing**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Command: `systemctl restart tomcat9`
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Verify application logs for clean startup without Log4j2 lookup errors.
